<title>Global Crude Oil Price Trends: A Historical Analysis (1970–2026)</title>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.0/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --bg2: #161b27;
    --bg3: #1e2538;
    --accent: #e8a020;
    --accent2: #f0c060;
    --red: #e05555;
    --green: #48c78e;
    --blue: #5b9cf6;
    --muted: #8892a4;
    --text: #e2e8f0;
    --border: #2a3350;
    --radius: 10px;
    --font: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }

  /* HEADER */
  .report-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0b1120 0%, #1a2540 60%, #0f1a30 100%);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 52px 60px 40px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .report-header::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      transparent,
      transparent 80px,
      rgba(232,160,32,0.03) 80px,
      rgba(232,160,32,0.03) 81px
    );
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .report-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(232,160,32,0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 4px 14px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(232,160,32,0.3);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .report-header h1 {
    font-size: 34px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: #fff;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .report-header h1 span { color: var(--accent); }
  .report-subtitle {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .report-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 28px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .meta-label { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .meta-value { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }

  /* LAYOUT */
  .container { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 40px 60px; }
  .section { margin-top: 52px; }
  .section-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .section-num {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
  }

  /* KPI CARDS */
  .kpi-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .kpi-card {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 20px 18px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .kpi-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .kpi-card.blue::before { background: var(--blue); }
  .kpi-card.green::before { background: var(--green); }
  .kpi-card.red::before { background: var(--red); }
  .kpi-card.purple::before { background: #a78bfa; }
  .kpi-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .kpi-value {
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #fff;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .kpi-sub {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* CHART CONTAINER */
  .chart-wrap {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 28px 24px 20px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .chart-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .chart-sub {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  /* TEXT BLOCKS */
  .analysis-block {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 24px 28px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .analysis-block p {
    color: #b8c5d8;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .analysis-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .highlight {
    color: var(--accent2);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .highlight-red { color: var(--red); font-weight: 600; }
  .highlight-green { color: var(--green); font-weight: 600; }

  /* TABLES */
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .data-table th {
    background: var(--bg3);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .data-table td {
    padding: 11px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(42,51,80,0.5);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .data-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .data-table tr:hover td { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); }
  .table-wrap {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .badge-up { background: rgba(72,199,142,0.15); color: var(--green); }
  .badge-down { background: rgba(224,85,85,0.15); color: var(--red); }
  .badge-neutral { background: rgba(91,156,246,0.15); color: var(--blue); }

  /* DECADE GRID */
  .decade-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .decade-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .decade-card {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 20px;
  }
  .decade-card .decade-name {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .decade-card .decade-avg {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
  }
  .decade-card .decade-meta {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .decade-bar-track {
    background: var(--bg3);
    border-radius: 4px;
    height: 6px;
    width: 100%;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .decade-bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2));
    transition: width 0.4s ease;
  }
  .decade-event {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .decade-event strong { color: var(--text); }

  /* SHOCK TABLE */
  .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* DISTRIBUTION */
  .stat-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .stat-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .stat-box {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stat-box .sv { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 800; color: #fff; }
  .stat-box .sl { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 4px; }

  /* FOOTER */
  .report-footer {
    margin-top: 60px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 24px 0;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  /* ANNOTATION TOOLTIP */
  .event-annotations {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .evt-tag {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    background: var(--bg3);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .evt-dot {
    width: 8px; height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .callout {
    background: rgba(232,160,32,0.06);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 16px 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: #c8d4e8;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .callout strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .insight-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .insight-row .chart-wrap { flex: 2; }
  .insight-row .analysis-block { flex: 1; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="report-tag">Trend Analysis Report</div>
  <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends:<br><span>A Historical Analysis (1970–2026)</span></h1>
  <p class="report-subtitle">
    A comprehensive examination of monthly crude oil prices over 56 years — surfacing structural regimes,
    price shocks, volatility patterns, and long-run growth dynamics across the global energy market.
  </p>
  <div class="report-meta">
    <div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Data Source</span><span class="meta-value">Global Fuel Price Trends 1970–2026</span></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Observations</span><span class="meta-value">675 Monthly Records</span></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Coverage</span><span class="meta-value">January 1970 – March 2026</span></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Unit</span><span class="meta-value">USD per Barrel (Nominal)</span></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Report Date</span><span class="meta-value">April 2026</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- ============================================================
     SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW
     ============================================================ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">01</span>
    <span class="section-title">Executive Overview</span>
  </div>

  <!-- KPI CARDS -->
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Price Range (Min → Max)</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$131.62</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">$1.21 (Jan 1970) → $132.83 (Jul 2008)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card blue">
      <div class="kpi-label">CAGR (56.2 Years)</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">7.93%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">$1.21 → $87.84 · Jan 1970 to Mar 2026</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card red">
      <div class="kpi-label">Peak Monthly Drop</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">−$26.96</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sep → Oct 2008 · Financial Crisis</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">Highest-Avg Decade</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">2010s</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Avg $76.45/bbl · High-price supercycle</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card purple">
      <div class="kpi-label">Overall Std Deviation</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$30.61</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sample std dev across 675 observations</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="analysis-block">
    <p>
      Over 56 years of monthly data, global crude oil prices have risen from a baseline of
      <span class="highlight">$1.21/bbl in January 1970</span> to <span class="highlight">$87.84/bbl in March 2026</span>,
      representing a compound annual growth rate of <span class="highlight">7.93%</span> — but this linear framing
      obscures the true nature of crude pricing: a series of discrete structural regimes punctuated by violent shocks.
    </p>
    <p>
      The dataset spans five complete decades and part of a sixth. The mean price across all 675 observations is
      <span class="highlight">$39.80/bbl</span>, yet the median is only <span class="highlight">$29.11/bbl</span> —
      a $10.69 gap indicating strong right-skewness driven by the post-2004 supercycle. The standard deviation of
      $30.61 is 77% of the mean, underscoring extreme distributional spread relative to central tendency.
    </p>
    <p>
      Three defining macro-events dominate the 56-year arc: the <span class="highlight">1973–74 OPEC Embargo</span>
      (prices tripled in a single month), the <span class="highlight">2008 commodity boom and financial crisis collapse</span>
      (prices reached $132.83 before crashing 69% in five months), and the <span class="highlight">2020 COVID-19 demand shock</span>
      (the fastest-ever peacetime demand collapse). The 2022 Russia-Ukraine war spike and the anomalous March 2026 surge
      represent the most recent structural disruptions visible in the data.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================
     SECTION 2: LONG-TERM PRICE TRAJECTORY
     ============================================================ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">02</span>
    <span class="section-title">Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</span>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <div class="chart-title">Monthly Crude Oil Price — January 1970 to March 2026</div>
    <div class="chart-sub">USD per barrel (nominal) · 675 monthly observations · Key events annotated</div>
    <canvas id="mainChart" style="height: 400px;"></canvas>
    <div class="event-annotations" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#e8a020;"></div>1973–74 OPEC Embargo</div>
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#f0c060;"></div>1979 Iranian Revolution</div>
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#5b9cf6;"></div>1986 Price Collapse</div>
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#a78bfa;"></div>1990 Gulf War</div>
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#48c78e;"></div>2008 Peak / GFC</div>
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#e05555;"></div>2020 COVID Shock</div>
      <div class="evt-tag"><div class="evt-dot" style="background:#fb7185;"></div>2022 Russia-Ukraine</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="analysis-block">
    <p>
      The long-run trajectory reveals four distinct price regimes. The <strong style="color:var(--text)">Pre-Shock Era (1970–1972)</strong>
      was characterized by remarkable stability: prices were anchored at $1.21/bbl for the entirety of 1970, creeping up
      modestly to $1.87 by mid-1972 as production quotas held.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <strong style="color:var(--text)">Shock-and-Rebalance Era (1973–1999)</strong> opened with the most dramatic single-month move
      in the entire dataset: <span class="highlight-red">December 1973 to January 1974 saw prices leap from $4.10 to $13.00 (+217%)</span>,
      the direct result of the OPEC embargo. A second shock followed in 1979 when the Iranian Revolution drove prices to $40.75/bbl by
      November 1979. The ensuing 1980s saw a gradual unwind and then a sharp collapse: by July 1986 prices had fallen to $9.62/bbl
      as OPEC abandoned its output ceiling, representing an 84% decline from the 1980 peak. The 1990s were a relatively stable,
      low-price period (mean: $18.19/bbl) interrupted only briefly by the Gulf War spike of August–October 1990.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <strong style="color:var(--text)">Supercycle (2000–2014)</strong> represents the most sustained bull market in crude history.
      Driven by Chinese demand growth, financial commodities flows, and geopolitical risk premia, prices rose from $25/bbl in 2000
      to a peak of <span class="highlight">$132.83/bbl in July 2008</span>. The financial crisis produced the sharpest absolute
      drawdown: $132.83 to $41.34 in just five months (Aug–Dec 2008), a 68.9% collapse. Recovery was swift — prices were back above
      $80 by late 2009 and sustained above $100 from 2011 to mid-2014.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <strong style="color:var(--text)">Post-Supercycle Volatility Era (2014–2026)</strong> has been defined by multiple
      structural dislocations: the 2014–16 shale-driven collapse (from $108 to $27/bbl), the 2020 COVID demand shock
      (prices briefly hit $21.04 in April 2020, the lowest since 2002), the 2021–22 recovery and Ukraine-war spike
      (touching $116.80 in June 2022), and a subsequent gradual normalization toward the $60–90 range.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

